tectural Designs"] "”, were identical, but were assessed separately for both categories. Therefore, works that were not awarded with a medal " [:a {:href "/results/920032"} "cannot be attributed to either category"] "."] "\n\n" [:p {} "In architecture, all six medals were awarded. Probably for the first time, so-called “Honorable Mentions” were also expressed. The jury for architecture consisted of mostly well known architects from the USA."] "\n\n" [:p {} "British architect " [:a {:href "/athletes/920494"} "John Hughes"] " won the gold medal for " [:em {} "Design of a Sports and Recreation Centre with Stadium for the City of Liverpool"] ". His design, however, was not realized."] "\n\n" [:p {} "The silver medalist was Danish architect " [:a {:href "/athletes/920224"} "Jens Houmøller Klemmensen"] ", with his " [:em {} "Stadium and Public Park"] ". " [:em {} "Marathon Park"] ", which won the bronze medal, was the work of Belgian architect " [:a {:href "/athletes/920174"} "André Verbeke"] "."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Catalogue Number"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Translated Title"] [:th {} "Original Title"] [:th {} "Title in Olympic Report or Catalogue"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "270"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/920494"} "John Hughes"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GBR"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/GBR.png"}] "GBR"]] [:td {} "Design of a Sports and Recreation Centre with Stadium for the City of Liverpool"] [:td {} "Design of a Sports and Recreation Centre with Stadium for the City of Liverpool"] [:td {} "Sports and Recreation Center with Stadium for the City of Liverpool"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "199"] [:td {} [:a {:href "